KNOWNBUG (sizeof... in a static data member initializer): [temp.variadic]/8
`sizeof...(T)` must be the pack's element count.  In a member function body this
is correct (works), but in a static data member initializer the pack is
collapsed during class-template instantiation, so the count is wrong for both
multi-element and empty packs.  Part of the unified pack-expansion rework
documented in doc/architectural/cpp-variadic-pack-expansion-rework.md.
Reclassify CORE once sizeof... is evaluated against the full pack here.
